  "answer": "**Final status: passing.** One fix was needed. On the second run, build, unit and component tests all passed (run `20261021T111825Z-dd1bde`, summary at `tmp/verification/20261021T111825Z-dd1bde/summary.json`).\n\n**What failed:** On the first run the build passed but the unit tests failed. Component tests were skipped because of that. One unit test failed on both net9.0 and net10.0: `DeltaFormatterTests.Format_FieldInActualNotInExpected_ShowsAbsentSentinel`. It was a failed assertion, not a compile error. The test expected `<absent>` in the output but got `expected: <not present>`.\n\n**Root cause:** `src/ConfIT/Matching/DeltaFormatter.cs` used the wrong placeholder text. When a field is in the actual response but not in the expected one, it printed `<not present>`. The docs (`doc/failure-output.md`, `CHANGELOG.md`, the skills' `writing-tests.md` and the `.lattice` context doc) all say `<absent>`. The test was right and the code was wrong.\n\n**What changed:** One string at `src/ConfIT/Matching/DeltaFormatter.cs:69`: `TestColor.Subtle(\"<not present>\")` became `TestColor.Subtle(\"<absent>\")`. The test files were not touched.\n\nThe verification config only runs build, unit and component tests, so integration tests and `make skills` (both part of `make ci`) were not run. Nothing has been committed.",
